  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Reported by Nigel Thomas",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Concurrent policy modifications and reads cause deadlocks with DBXML.  ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The current FeSL code does not manage deadlocks (or even attempt to detect them).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This can result in a corrupt policy index, or a \"permanent deadlock\" state where restarting the Fedora server fails to clear the DBXML deadlock - so first access to the repository never completes.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Attached are amended versions of DbXmlManager and DbXmlPolicyIndex that include wrapping operations in transactions, detection of deadlocks and transaction abortion when deadlocks occur (against release 3.4.1).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
